    "description": "PARKED — the Drive project builds the NEW pipeline only. It does not move the 400GB+ already sitting in Dropbox.\n\nWhat that means in practice until a migration decision is made:\n\n* Dropbox keeps running and keeps being billed\n\n* HISTORICAL PROOF LINKS STAY PUBLICLY ACCESSIBLE — the current links are public, never expire, and run through a single admin-owned token\n\n* Everything in the Drive plan applies to NEW proofs only\n\n* Treat migration and decommissioning as its own decision once the Drive pipeline is proven, and scope it then\n\n* WORTH RAISING WITH WAGERTECH SEPARATELY: the public-link exposure on historical files is a live access-control issue regardless of whether migration is deferred. Better access control is one of the stated drivers for the Drive move, and it does not arrive for existing files until this is done\n\nSource: Drive Storage doc §9, §1.",
